# Cloudflare Pages reads this file and applies these headers to the deploy.
#
# Everything revalidates. That is deliberate, and it is not the usual advice.
#
# The usual advice for a static site is to fingerprint asset filenames and then
# serve them `immutable` for a year. Meadowline cannot do that: it has no build
# step, and its 139 source modules are imported by bare path from one another
# (`import { S } from '../core/state.js'`). Only index.html's own seven URLs
# carry the ?v= release tag. Marking /src/* immutable would therefore pin every
# player to whatever JavaScript they happened to load first, permanently, and
# the failure would be silent — a fixed bug that never goes away for anyone who
# already visited. `tests/build-tag-regression.html` fails the build if anyone
# adds a long cache to a path whose URLs are not version-stamped.
#
# `no-cache` does not mean "do not cache". It means "cache it, then ask before
# reusing it". Every request becomes a conditional one and almost all of them
# come back 304 Not Modified with no body, so this costs a round trip rather
# than a download — the right trade for a game that is patched often and whose
# largest file is a few hundred kilobytes.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# The page itself must never be held, or a player never even learns that a new
# release tag exists and the versioned URLs below are never requested.
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
